{{also|Locket}}
==English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|fr|en}} {{m|fr|loquet}}, from a diminutive of {{etyl|xno|en}} {{m|fro|loc}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|en-us-locket.ogg|Audio (US)|lang=en}}
* {{rhymes|ɒkɪt|lang=en}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# A [[pendant]] that opens to reveal a space used for storing a [[photograph]] or other small item.
# {{lb|en|archaic}} The upper metallic cap of a sword’s [[scabbard]].
# A small white [[marking]] on a cat's [[coat]].

